     "approved_version": "The payroll with each worker's hours, pieces, deductions and net pay exactly as checked by the contractor in s7, released once to the bank; any change needs a new check.",
     "approval_step_id": "s7",
     "approver": "farm labor contractor"
    }
   ],
   "design": "Foremen record hours and piece counts per worker in a phone app that feeds payroll software; the software applies hourly and piece rates and flags pay below the minimum wage, so sheets are not collected, typed or calculated by hand. Payslips go to workers' phones and the software keeps the records. Deduction checks, disputes, the payroll check, releasing payments and explaining pay stay with the contractor; no decision on pay is made by software alone.",
   "previous_blocker": "Paper sheets were collected, typed and calculated each week.",
   "enabler_now": "Phone time recording and payroll software with piece rates.",
   "still_hard": "Workers without smartphones and disputed counts.",
   "human_edge": "Settling a pay dispute fairly in the field.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less collecting and typing; disputes and checks stay.",
   "reach": [
